<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 114,049 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 114,049 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 114,049 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Friday compared to 96,466 tonnes in the same period on Thursday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Friday	Feb 27</p>
<p>    Export cargo		36,365	30,126</p>
<p>    Import cargo		77,684	66,340</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and two berthed. In the next 24 hours, six are expected to sail and five are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Palm oil		 16,500	 Bunga Cenderewasih 28/2</p>
<p>Chemicals		 9,900	 NCC Najd		1/3</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     27,000	 Philadelphia	  4/3</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros-I	     4/3</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     22,649	 Seram		   8/3</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
